  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Find $a$ and $b$ if $ax-10y=8$ and $6x+by=12$ represent the same line.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=4$, $b=-15$.",
      "worked": "The equations represent the same line, so multiplying the first equation by $\\frac{12}{8}=\\frac32$ must give the second equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac32(ax-10y)&=\\frac32\\times8\\\\\\frac{3a}{2}x-15y&=12\\end{align*}$$\n\nComparing coefficients with $6x+by=12$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3a}{2}&=6\\\\a&=4\\\\b&=-15\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck: multiplying $4x-10y=8$ by $\\frac32$ gives $6x-15y=12$, as required.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
